# ── PRM form submission ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Oldham runs in PROXIED mode: forms POST same-origin to /api/prm/* and the
# route handlers inject the TDS key server-side, so the key NEVER ships to the
# browser. Set these in the Vercel project (Production AND Preview):
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PRM_PROXY_BASE=/api/prm   ← turns on proxied mode (client-visible, safe)
#   TDS_API_KEY=<scoped TDS submission key>   ← SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never prefix NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PRM_ACCOUNT_ID=<account id>   ← public, used for file uploads
#
# Do NOT set NEXT_PUBLIC_TDS_API_KEY in proxied mode — it would inline the key
# into the shipped HTML/JS and defeat the whole point of the proxy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRM_PROXY_BASE=/api/prm
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRM_ACCOUNT_ID=
TDS_API_KEY=

# ── DIRECT mode (fallback only — e.g. a host with no serverless functions) ──
# Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_PRM_PROXY_BASE blank and set these instead. The key WILL be
# public in the browser bundle. Not used on Vercel.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRM_ENDPOINT=https://prm.tio.work/api/xcms-to-prm-v4-tds
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TDS_API_KEY=

# ── Analytics (supplied by the practice — see Analytics.tsx) ────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
